{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f879536012842e8ddc896470e33cfa63fca6e6aa9baaef0d4065f2f38e176c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI argument parser","key_entities":["rebar comment","rebar create","rebar edit","rebar session-log","rebar tag","rebar untag","rebar archive","rebar set-verify-commands","--body-file","--body","--","args[:min_args]"],"problem_keywords":["silent flag consumption","positional argument parsing","CLI argument validation","command body loss","exit code 0 on error","durability","flag-like body content"],"propositions":["rebar comment accepts flag-like tokens (--body-file, --body) as positional body content and stores them literally, silently discarding the actual intended body.","Commands with positional body arguments silently accept and consume flag-like tokens starting with `-` and exit with code 0, making the data loss undetectable until content is read back.","A user-provided body that legitimately begins with `-` must be writable via a documented escape hatch (--) without flag interpretation.","All positional-body commands (comment, create, edit, session-log, tag, untag, archive, set-verify-commands) must reject flag-like argument patterns with non-zero exit and a corrective usage message."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787314462925753001,"uuid":"ad6e9185-4631-40a8-b8e1-a3973754a925"}